## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical asynchronous processing, per-tenant isolation, idempotency, and multi-env deployment in a beginner-friendly Azure setup.

## Key Concepts

- HTTP-triggered Functions
- Azure Service Bus
- JWT-based tenantId extraction
- Idempotency keys and Redis deduplication
- Per-tenant storage isolation
- GitHub Actions multi-env

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: extract tenant, deduplicate, enqueue
async function processRequest(req) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  const tenantId = decodeJWT(token).tenantId;
  const idem = req.headers['x-idempotency-key'] ?? require('uuid').v4();
  if (await redis.exists(`idem:${tenantId}:${idem}`)) throw new Error('Duplicate');
  await redis.set(`idem:${tenantId}:${idem}`, '1', 'EX', 86400);
  const msg = { tenantId, ...req.body, id: uuid() };
  await serviceBus.send(queue, msg);
  return { status: 202 };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency under retries?
- How would you monitor cross-tenant latency and failures?

